  "notes": "Result: 10 of 10 rows are correct. 0 rows are imprecise. 0 rows are wrong. Method: read only. For each name I ran git grep (the doc file excluded), followed the constants and helper functions that hold the name, and read the code around every read and set. Every quoted log text, default, accepted value and exit status in the 10 rows was found in the source. Sources outside the repository: (1) The spdlog level names and the SPDLOG_LEVEL rules for TRON_LOG_LEVEL come from spdlog v1.17.0, the version pinned in cmake/versions.cmake line 5. I read a local copy of that version at /home/jhan/workspace/tron/gen/_deps/spdlog-src (include/spdlog/common-inl.h from_str, cfg/helpers-inl.h load_levels, details/registry-inl.h set_levels). (2) The RZ_CLI_ARGS statements on word splitting of the form $VAR and on the order of EnvironmentFile lines rest on the systemd manual pages systemd.service(5) and systemd.exec(5). I did not run systemd. (3) The statement that GitHub Actions runner images define ImageOS is a fact about GitHub. The repository holds no evidence for or against it. Details that the rows leave out. None contradicts the code and none is graded as a problem: (a) PROMPT_MODE: an empty value behaves like unset and gives `long`, because the script uses ${PROMPT_MODE:-long} (perfetto/tools/burst-test.sh:28). The row states only the unset case. A possible addition is 'Unset or empty: `long`.' (b) DICE_DAEMON_CHILD: the wrappers and `bin/slice` start the work directly only after the Dice daemon accepts a `grant-check` request with DICE_GRANT_ID, DICE_GRANT_TOKEN and DICE_SLOTS. A missing id or token, or a rejected check, ends the command with exit status 2 (bin/rinzler:478-503, bin/slice:5109-5129). The row is 987 characters long, so there is little room to add this. (c) TRON_HW_SAMPLER: perfetto/grant-rapl-read runs `sudo -n chmod a+r` only when at least one RAPL file is not readable. The option -n never asks for a password. When sudo fails, the script prints a warning with the manual command (perfetto/grant-rapl-read:35-46). (d) LSB_HOSTS: the runner cuts each name at the first dot. A name that is not a valid host name fails the check (bin/dice_lsf.py:140-144)."
